{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/703215-questions-about-dream-form-stats-and-the-primordial-dream","id":703215,"title":"Questions About Dream Form Stats And The Primordial Dream","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-16T05:10:11-07:00","id":703215,"title":"Questions About Dream Form Stats And The Primordial Dream","content":"The Kickstarter says that the Dream Health of mortals and most supernatural characters is Resolve + Attribute Maximum, and gives the example of a Beast who has Resolve 3 and Lair 6, thus Dream Health 9. However, it also says that the Horror uses Power, Finesse and Resistance like an ephemeral being. A Beast gets Lair x 2 dots to distribute among these ephemeral attributes plus Size. But if Dream Health is not linked to Size, and the Horror's Resistance stands in for Resolve, why would I spend dots on the Horror's Size? The only benefit would be making the Horror more resistant against the Stunned Tilt. I'm guessing the example was merely illustrative, and that the Dream Health of Beasts/Horrors would be Resistance + Size. The default Size of Horrors is not specified, but I assume it is the same as that of an adult human, which is 5. Furthermore, no upper limit for the attributes of the Horror is mentioned. Does that mean a Horror can have its attributes exceed the Lair rating and even go beyond 10? I also remember that Beasts who open Primordial Pathways (and thus reveal their true forms) can spend willpower points instead of Satiety to improve Atavisms, but I can't find the part of Kickstarter that says this.<br /> <br /> On a related note, Demons who know the &quot;Rip The Gates&quot; Exploit can enter the Astral, but can they invade the Primordial Dream? They enter the Astral as physical beings, so I assume they keep the 9 attributes of a material being. <br /> <br /> But what about Mages? They can reach the three layers of the Astral as a template ability, but is there anything explicitly barring their way into the Primordial Dream? It is located inside the Temenos and is close to the Anima Mundi, so perhaps the Ecstatic Wind is present?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-16T07:00:18-07:00","id":703368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/703215-questions-about-dream-form-stats-and-the-primordial-dream#post703215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> But if Dream Health is not linked to Size, and the Horror's Resistance stands in for Resolve, why would I spend dots on the Horror's Size?</div> </div> </div> </div> There are Lair traits that work off Size. There are also other abilities - Cyclopean Strength, Looming Presence, and Titanic Blow - that use Size. I'm sure that the ST can use other ruels that involve Size, such as trying to crush someone with your weight or use it for leverage, or some other Conditions/Tilts. You also mentioned the Stunned Tilt. In general, growing in Size without gaining extra Health is a thing for the Giant Family, so that's most likely why.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On a related note, Demons who know the &quot;Rip The Gates&quot; Exploit can enter the Astral, but can they invade the Primordial Dream? They enter the Astral as physical beings, so I assume they keep the 9 attributes of a material being. </div> </div> </div>The primordial dream is part of the astral. So, yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But what about Mages? They can reach the three layers of the Astral as a template ability, but is there anything explicitly barring their way into the Primordial Dream? It is located inside the Temenos and is close to the Anima Mundi, so perhaps the Ecstatic Wind is present? </div> </div> </div> Lets wait until 2e comes out before we start making calls about mages and the Astral. That could very well have changed from 1e, with how the Supernal is no longer Astral Level 4, and more of a &quot;realm of the Mind.&quot; Things change.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-16T09:32:39-07:00","id":703599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/703215-questions-about-dream-form-stats-and-the-primordial-dream#post703215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a related note, Demons who know the &quot;Rip The Gates&quot; Exploit can enter the Astral, but can they invade the Primordial Dream? They enter the Astral as physical beings, so I assume they keep the 9 attributes of a material being.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But what about Mages? They can reach the three layers of the Astral as a template ability, but is there anything explicitly barring their way into the Primordial Dream? It is located inside the Temenos and is close to the Anima Mundi, so perhaps the Ecstatic Wind is present? </div> </div> </div>Mages have a bit of a home-ground advantage in the astral, though not as much as Beasts - they use the higher of their Social or Mental stats for each of Power, Finesse, and Resistance in dream form (every else just uses their Mental stats) and they have their Amnions, astral Mage Armor.<br /> <br /> The Primordial Dream is in the deep Temenos - to get to it as a mage, you go up to the Boundary Stone between the Temenos and Anima Mundi and go exploring off to the side instead of Speaking the Stone open and passing through into the Anima Mundi. (the Stone is the Temenos realm of High Speech, and therefore Language, it's symbolically what separates humans from everything else).<br /> <br /> Beasts are nightmares, but they're *human* nightmares, and they're in the human side of that boundary. There's no ecstatic wind in the PD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-16T18:27:41-07:00","id":704081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/703215-questions-about-dream-form-stats-and-the-primordial-dream?p=703599#post703599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. . . Mages have a bit of a home-ground advantage in the astral, though not as much as Beasts . . .<br /> <br /> The Primordial Dream is in the deep Temenos - to get to it as a mage . . .<br /> <br /> Beasts are nightmares, but they're *human* nightmares, and they're in the human side of that boundary. . .</div> </div> </div> </div>Perfect! <b>Dave</b>, if you have a moment, any thoughts on how the Dreamspeakers fit in? Are Horrors/Souls a form of Dreamborn? Are Primals* going to show up in my Lair, wanting directions? Is a Chamber a type of Dreamland?<br /> <br /> <br /> *the nickname for mages in the Dreamspeaker Legacy<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-16T20:30:52-07:00","id":704231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/703215-questions-about-dream-form-stats-and-the-primordial-dream?p=704081#post704081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are Horrors/Souls a form of Dreamborn? [\u2026] Is a Chamber a type of Dreamland?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The Anima Mundi&quot; and &quot;The Dreamtime&quot; are synonyms. Dreamborn occupy places in the Dreamtime and the Primordial Dream is in the Temenos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}